What:		/sys/class/qcom-battery/charge_counter
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only remaining battery charge in microamp-hours, exposed for
		Xiaomi MiCharge clients that use the qcom-battery class path.
		It reads POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER from the same battery
		power_supply as /sys/class/power_supply/battery/charge_counter.
		Backend failures are returned to the reader; the attribute does
		not substitute capacity percentages or synthesized charge values.

What:		/sys/class/qcom-battery/board_sensor_temp
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only board virtual temperature in millidegrees Celsius. Reads
		the same mutex-protected sample published by the Venus userspace
		thermal model to thermal_message/board_sensor_temp. An unpublished
		sample or one older than 30 seconds returns ENODATA (including time
		spent suspended); malformed or overflowing text returns the
		integer parser's error. This is not an independent physical sensor
		and does not compute or fabricate an initial temperature. The
		userspace producer must be restored when absent from a ported ROM.
		The thermal_message reader applies the same validity check. A new
		valid write refreshes its timestamp; invalid text invalidates it.
